cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this work, please cite it as below.
title: 'DesignLab: conservation-aware PCR and qPCR primer design across homologous sequences'
type: software
authors:
- given-names: Gültekin
  family-names: Ünal
  orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8996-7028
  affiliation: Ankara University, Faculty of Veterinary Medicine, Department of Microbiology
abstract: A browser-based tool that takes a gene sequence or a gene name, retrieves
  homologous records from NCBI, aligns them with MAFFT, locates the conserved blocks
  and lets Primer3 place primers only inside those blocks. Every oligo is then checked
  base by base against every downloaded sequence, and each binding site is drawn on
  the alignment with its mismatches. Base-pairing geometry is computed by the tool;
  thermodynamic values come from Primer3 alone. Research use only; primers are not
  validated for diagnostic use without wet-lab confirmation.
repository-code: https://github.com/cinnetcrash/designlab
url: https://github.com/cinnetcrash/designlab
license: MIT
